46,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
48,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The candidates are A: Meridian, B: Tessera, C: Corvus, and D: Anchor. I lean toward A for the regional service team and fixed configuration.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,D is the only one that feels real. On-site engineers and a system built for transport operators is exactly what the depots need.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,3,1,talk,May,,"B relies on a partner for migration, which I distrust. C is too modular and likely to age poorly. I prefer D for the engineering presence.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Misaki,,A and B seem too detached. D's on-site team during rollout helps solve the supervisor training problem I found.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"C's modular licensing is a financial trap. A is hosted, but D's on-site server model is a capital expense the board might dislike, though maintenance is stable.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, do you think Anchor's on-site deployment would interfere with the peak-season cutover?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, having their engineers actually here means they can't just point fingers during an outage. It's safer than a remote team.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, would the board prefer a one-time purchase for D over the creeping costs of a subscription like B?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, a fixed configuration in A might be too rigid if the business rules change every few months.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,3,talk,Midori,,"That's a fair point, Misaki. If the scope doesn't survive a year, a ""fixed"" process is a liability.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,D is the most robust choice for the yard. I'm voting for Anchor.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,3,talk,May,,I agree with Ryuji. The engineering team on-site is the only way to ensure the data lift is done right.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm voting for D as well. It's the best way to support the crews and the remaining admins.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I've changed my mind. Given the need for accountability and flexibility, D is the strongest option. I vote D.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,4,pass,Ryuji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
63,3,4,pass,May,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
64,3,4,pass,Misaki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While the capital request is a hurdle, the long-term cost stability of D outweighs the risks of A or B. I vote D.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
